Definitions:

```
/-- The unit (n-1)-sphere. -/
abbrev ModelSphere (n : ℕ) := {x : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) // ‖x‖ = 1}

/-- The model space form of curvature K and dimension n: polar coordinate patch ℝ × S^{n-1}. -/
abbrev ModelSpace (n : ℕ) := ℝ × ModelSphere n

/-- Tangent vectors at a model point, represented in ambient coordinates
(ℝ along the radial direction times the ambient Euclidean space of the sphere). -/
abbrev ModelTangent (n : ℕ) := ℝ × EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)

/-- The warped-product metric in polar form: g((a,x),(b,y)) = a b + j_K(r)² ⟨x,y⟩. -/
noncomputable def modelMetric (K : ℝ) (n : ℕ) (r : ℝ) : ModelTangent n → ModelTangent n → ℝ :=
  fun X Y => X.1 * Y.1 + jacobiSol K r ^ 2 * inner ℝ X.2 Y.2
```

n = dimension; n = 0/1 degenerate but definitions still make sense. For n = 1: sphere S⁰ ⊆ ℝ — ‖x‖ = 1 two points; fine.

